--Description:
-- The earlier step tried to extract a readable county name from the ACS table via a 
-- non-existent column called `name`.  Because that column isn’t present, we can instead
-- obtain clean county names directly from the vaccination-site table.  Each record’s 
-- `facility_sub_region_2` field contains a string such as “Los Angeles County”.  
-- The query below lists distinct county strings for California and removes the 
-- trailing word “ County” so we have a tidy county label that can be used for joins.

SELECT DISTINCT
  facility_sub_region_2                           AS county_raw,           -- e.g. "Los Angeles County"
  REGEXP_REPLACE(facility_sub_region_2,
                 r' County$', '')                 AS county_clean          -- e.g. "Los Angeles"
FROM `bigquery-public-data.covid19_vaccination_access.facility_boundary_us_all`
WHERE facility_sub_region_1 = 'California'
LIMIT 20;
```
